# Messenger API: auth and users
# Replace the empty variables before sending protected requests.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@accessToken =
@refreshToken =
@searchQuery = andrei

### Health check
# Confirms that the Express server is running.
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Register a user
# Creates a user. Change username and email before re-sending: both must be unique.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Andrei",
  "username": "andrei",
  "email": "andrei@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login
# identifier accepts either username or email.
# Copy accessToken from the JSON response into @accessToken.
# Copy refreshToken from the Set-Cookie response header into @refreshToken.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "andrei",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Current authenticated user
# Requires a valid access JWT. Returns 401 when the token is missing, invalid, or expired.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh access token
# Sends the refresh token as a cookie and returns a new 15-minute access token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Cookie: refreshToken={{refreshToken}}

### Logout
# Deletes the refresh session and clears the refresh-token cookie. Returns 204 with no body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Cookie: refreshToken={{refreshToken}}

### Search users by username
# q is optional: an empty q returns an empty users array.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/search?q={{searchQuery}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get all users (development endpoint)
# Warning: this route currently returns Prisma User records without a select/omit filter.
# Do not use it as a client-facing endpoint until sensitive fields are explicitly excluded.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
